[6.394224, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/FEATURES.md\n"]
[6.394464, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/FEATURES.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[6.395989, "o", "# Churn model features: specification\r\n\r\nOwner: retention data science. This is the contract between the feature pipeline (`python -m churn.build_features`)\r\nand the churn model (`python -m churn.train`). The live scoring service computes the same features from the same\r\ndefinitions, so offline and live values must agree.\r\n\r\n## The one rule\r\nEach output row is one prediction for one customer at one moment `t` (the row's `as_of`). **A feature for that row may\r\nuse only information that existed strictly before `t`.** The definitions below say exactly what that means for each\r\nfeature; where they are more specific, they win.\r\n\r\n## Conventions\r\n- All timestamps are UTC, written as ISO 8601 with a `Z` suffix and whole seconds (`2025-03-04T06:00:00Z`).\r\n- \"Day\" means a UTC calendar date. `date(t)` is the UTC date of `t`.\r\n- \"In days\" means elapsed seconds divided by 86,400 (a fractional number).\r\n- `W days` means exactly `W × 86,400` seconds.\r\n- Windows are half-open: `[t − W days, t)` contains an event at exact"]
[6.396086, "o", "ly `t − W days` and does **not** contain an event at\r\n  exactly `t`. Events are stamped to the second, and an event stamped exactly at `t` (for example the box charge that\r\n  the 06:00 billing run creates while the 06:00 scoring run is reading) is not visible to the prediction at `t`.\r\n\r\n## Input tables (`--data <dir>`)\r\n| File | Columns | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `customers.csv` | `customer_id, signup_at, plan, postcode_district` | one row per customer |\r\n| `scoring_points.csv` | `customer_id, as_of, trigger, app_minutes_7d` | one row per prediction; `(customer_id, as_of)` is unique; `trigger` is `batch` (the 06:00 run) or `ticket` (scored by the support desk when a ticket is opened, at the ticket's `opened_at`); `app_minutes_7d` is the product-analytics reading for that prediction and is often empty (export outages, devices offline) |\r\n| `orders.csv` | `order_id, customer_id, ordered_at, kind, amount_cents` | `kind` is `box` or `addon`; amounts are integer cents |\r\n| `tickets.csv` | `ticket_id, customer_"]
[6.396154, "o", "id, opened_at, topic` | support tickets |\r\n| `status_snapshots.csv` | `customer_id, snapshot_date, status` | `snapshot_date` is a date (`YYYY-MM-DD`); at most one row per `(customer_id, snapshot_date)`; a snapshot dated `D` records the account status at the **end** of day `D`; `status` is one of `active`, `paused`, `payment_failed`, `cancelled` |\r\n| `labels.csv` | `customer_id, as_of, churned_30d, label_available_at` | one row per labelled prediction; `churned_30d` is 1 if the customer cancelled in `(as_of, as_of + 30 days]`, else 0; `label_available_at` is when that outcome landed in the warehouse. Predictions whose outcome had not landed when the extract was taken have no row. |\r\n\r\n## Output (`--out <file.parquet>`)\r\nOne row per row of `scoring_points.csv`, exactly once each, with these columns (row and column order do not matter):\r\n\r\n| Column | Type | Definition |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `customer_id` | integer | key, from `scoring_points.csv` |\r\n| `as_of` | timestamp (UTC) | key, `t` |\r\n| `orders_7d` | integer "]
[6.396209, "o", "| number of orders with `t − 7 days ≤ ordered_at < t` |\r\n| `orders_30d` | integer | number of orders with `t − 30 days ≤ ordered_at < t` |\r\n| `spend_30d_cents` | integer | sum of `amount_cents` over the same 30-day window; `0` when there are none |\r\n| `tickets_30d` | integer | number of tickets with `t − 30 days ≤ opened_at < t` |\r\n| `days_since_last_order` | float or null | `t` minus the latest `ordered_at` that is `< t`, in days; null when the customer has no earlier order |\r\n| `tenure_days` | float | `t − signup_at`, in days |\r\n| `status` | string or null | `status` of the customer's latest snapshot with `snapshot_date < date(t)`; null when there is none. (The snapshot dated `date(t)` describes the end of that day, so it does not exist yet at `t`.) |\r\n| `app_minutes_7d` | float or null | the row's own `app_minutes_7d` when present; otherwise the value of the same customer's most recent row with a strictly earlier `as_of` that has one; otherwise null. Never a value from a row at or after `t`. "]
[6.396285, "o", "|\r\n| `te_district` | float | target encoding of the customer's `postcode_district`, defined below |\r\n\r\n### `te_district`\r\nA label row is **available at `t`** when its `label_available_at < t`. For a prediction at `t` for a customer in\r\ndistrict `k`:\r\n- `p` = the mean of `churned_30d` over all label rows available at `t` (every district, every customer); if no label row\r\n  is available at `t`, `p = 0.05`.\r\n- `n` = the number of label rows available at `t` whose customer is in district `k` (this includes the same customer's\r\n  own earlier predictions whose outcome has landed); `s` = the sum of their `churned_30d`.\r\n- `te_district = (s + 20 × p) / (n + 20)`  (a smoothed mean with prior weight `m = 20`).\r\n\r\n## Run time\r\nA run on an extract of the size in `/app/data` (about 3,000 customers) must finish within the limit stated in the task\r\nticket.\r\n"]
[6.396422, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[6.770781, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/build_features.py\n"]
[6.771003, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/build_features.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[6.772305, "o", "\"\"\"Build the churn feature table: python -m churn.build_features --data <dir> --out <file.parquet>\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport os\r\n\r\nfrom churn.encoding import district_encoding\r\nfrom churn.impute import fill_app_minutes\r\nfrom churn.extract import load_extract\r\nfrom churn.status import latest_status\r\nfrom churn.windows import activity_features, tenure_days\r\n\r\nFEATURE_COLUMNS = [\"orders_7d\", \"orders_30d\", \"spend_30d_cents\", \"tickets_30d\", \"days_since_last_order\",\r\n                   \"tenure_days\", \"status\", \"app_minutes_7d\", \"te_district\"]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef build(data_dir):\r\n    t = load_extract(data_dir)\r\n"]
[6.772416, "o", "    points = t[\"scoring_points\"].reset_index(drop=True)\r\n    feats = activity_features(points, t[\"orders\"], t[\"tickets\"])\r\n    feats[\"tenure_days\"] = tenure_days(points, t[\"customers\"])\r\n    feats[\"status\"] = latest_status(points, t[\"status_snapshots\"])\r\n    feats[\"app_minutes_7d\"] = fill_app_minutes(points)\r\n    feats[\"te_district\"] = district_encoding(points, t[\"labels\"], t[\"customers\"])\r\n    return feats[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"] + FEATURE_COLUMNS]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data\", required=True, help=\"folder with the extract CSVs\")\r\n"]
[6.772474, "o", "    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"output parquet file\")\r\n    a = ap.parse_args()\r\n    feats = build(a.data)\r\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(a.out)), exist_ok=True)\r\n    feats.to_parquet(a.out, index=False)\r\n    print(f\"wrote {len(feats)} rows x {feats.shape[1]} columns to {a.out}\")\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"]
[6.772614, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[11.049577, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/windows.py\n"]
[11.049784, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/windows.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.05131, "o", "\"\"\"Activity features over trailing windows (orders, spend, tickets) and simple time-since features.\"\"\"\r\nimport numpy as np\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _daily(points, events, ts_col, amount_col=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Per customer and UTC day: number of events (and amount). Days that have a prediction but no event get 0.\"\"\"\r\n    ev = events.assign(day=events[ts_col].dt.floor(\"D\"))\r\n    agg = {\"n\": (ts_col, \"size\")}\r\n"]
[11.051425, "o", "    if amount_col:\r\n        agg[\"amount\"] = (amount_col, \"sum\")\r\n    per_day = ev.groupby([\"customer_id\", \"day\"]).agg(**agg).reset_index()\r\n    pred_days = points[[\"customer_id\"]].assign(day=points[\"as_of\"].dt.floor(\"D\")).drop_duplicates()\r\n    grid = pd.concat([per_day[[\"customer_id\", \"day\"]], pred_days]).drop_duplicates()\r\n    daily = grid.merge(per_day, on=[\"customer_id\", \"day\"], how=\"left\").fillna(0)\r\n    return daily.sort_values([\"customer_id\", \"day\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _rolling(daily, cols, window):\r\n    # daily buckets keep this fast; the window covers the last `window` including the prediction day\r\n"]
[11.05149, "o", "    rolled = (daily.set_index(\"day\").groupby(\"customer_id\")[cols]\r\n              .rolling(window, closed=\"both\").sum().reset_index())\r\n    return rolled\r\n\r\n\r\ndef activity_features(points, orders, tickets):\r\n    out = points[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"]].copy()\r\n    out[\"day\"] = out[\"as_of\"].dt.floor(\"D\")\r\n\r\n    od = _daily(points, orders, \"ordered_at\", \"amount_cents\")\r\n    r7 = _rolling(od, [\"n\"], \"7D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"orders_7d\"})\r\n    r30 = _rolling(od, [\"n\", \"amount\"], \"30D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"orders_30d\", \"amount\": \"spend_30d_cents\"})\r\n    td = _daily(points, tickets, \"opened_at\")\r\n    t30 = _rolling(td, [\"n\"], \"30D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"tickets_30d\"})\r\n    for part in (r7, r30, t30):\r\n        out = out.merge(part, on=[\"customer_id\", \"day\"], how=\"left\")\r\n    for c in (\"orders_7d\", \"orders_30d\", \"spend_30d_cents\", \"tickets_30d\"):\r\n        out[c] = out[c].fillna(0).astype(\"int64\")\r\n\r\n    # time since the last order strictly before the prediction\r\n    o = orders.sort_values(\"ordered_at\")[[\"customer_i"]
[11.051568, "o", "d\", \"ordered_at\"]]\r\n    left = out[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"]].reset_index().sort_values(\"as_of\")\r\n    last = pd.merge_asof(left, o, left_on=\"as_of\", right_on=\"ordered_at\", by=\"customer_id\",\r\n                         allow_exact_matches=False).set_index(\"index\").sort_index()[\"ordered_at\"]\r\n    out[\"days_since_last_order\"] = (out[\"as_of\"] - last).dt.total_seconds() / 86400\r\n    return out.drop(columns=[\"day\"])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef tenure_days(points, customers):\r\n    signup = points[\"customer_id\"].map(customers.set_index(\"customer_id\")[\"signup_at\"])\r\n    return (points[\"as_of\"] - signup).dt.total_seconds() / 86400\r\n"]
[11.051712, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.051788, "o", "root@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[11.566384, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/status.py\n"]
[11.566762, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/status.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.569317, "o", "\"\"\"Account status from the billing system's status snapshots.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef latest_status(points, snapshots):\r\n    \"\"\"Status of the customer's latest snapshot.\"\"\"\r\n    latest = (snapshots.sort_values([\"customer_id\", \"snapshot_date\"])\r\n              .drop_duplicates(\"customer_id\", keep=\"last\"))\r\n    return points[[\"customer_id\"]].merge(latest[[\"customer_id\", \"status\"]], on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\")[\"status\"]\r\n"]
[11.569641, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.569711, "o", "root@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[12.096914, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/impute.py\n"]
[12.097094, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/impute.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.098668, "o", "\"\"\"Gap filling for upstream readings that arrive with holes (analytics export outages, devices offline).\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef fill_app_minutes(points):\r\n    \"\"\"Fill missing app_minutes_7d from the nearest reading of the same customer.\"\"\"\r\n    pts = points.sort_values([\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"])\r\n"]
[12.098739, "o", "    filled = pts.groupby(\"customer_id\")[\"app_minutes_7d\"].transform(lambda s: s.bfill().ffill())\r\n    return filled.reindex(points.index)\r\n"]
[12.098931, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.098986, "o", "root@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[12.613228, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/encoding.py\n"]
[12.613654, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/encoding.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.615422, "o", "\"\"\"Target encoding of high-cardinality categoricals.\"\"\"\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\nPRIOR_WEIGHT = 20\r\nDEFAULT_PRIOR = 0.05\r\n\r\n\r\ndef district_encoding(points, labels, customers, m=PRIOR_WEIGHT):\r\n    \"\"\"Smoothed churn rate of the customer's postcode district.\"\"\"\r\n    district = customers.set_index(\"customer_id\")[\"postcode_district\"]\r\n    lab = labels.assign(district=labels[\"customer_id\"].map(district))\r\n    prior = lab[\"churned_30d\"].mean() if len(lab) else DEFAULT_PRIOR\r\n    stats = lab.groupby(\"district\")[\"churned_30d\"].agg([\"sum\", \"count\"])\r\n"]
[12.616307, "o", "    te = (stats[\"sum\"] + m * prior) / (stats[\"count\"] + m)\r\n    return points[\"customer_id\"].map(district).map(te).fillna(prior).astype(\"float64\")\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[13.13571, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/extract.py\n"]
[13.136116, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/extract.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.137712, "o", "\"\"\"Load a warehouse extract (the CSV layout described in FEATURES.md) into pandas frames with UTC timestamps.\"\"\"\r\nimport os\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\nTIMESTAMPS = {\r\n    \"customers\": [\"signup_at\"],\r\n    \"scoring_points\": [\"as_of\"],\r\n    \"orders\": [\"ordered_at\"],\r\n    \"tickets\": [\"opened_at\"],\r\n    \"status_snapshots\": [\"snapshot_date\"],\r\n    \"labels\": [\"as_of\", \"label_available_at\"],\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[13.137854, "o", "def load_extract(data_dir):\r\n    tables = {}\r\n    for name, cols in TIMESTAMPS.items():\r\n        df = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, f\"{name}.csv\"), dtype={\"postcode_district\": \"str\"})\r\n        for c in cols:\r\n            df[c] = pd.to_datetime(df[c], utc=True)\r\n        tables[name] = df\r\n    tables[\"scoring_points\"][\"app_minutes_7d\"] = tables[\"scoring_points\"][\"app_minutes_7d\"].astype(\"float64\")\r\n    return tables\r\n"]
[13.138117, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.138172, "o", "root@17a3e0e7-f835-42a4-9265-4eb0b35eea7d:/app# "]
[53.824186, "i", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch: churn/windows.py\n@@\n-\"\"\"Activity features over trailing windows (orders, spend, tickets) and simple time-since features.\"\"\"\n-import numpy as np\n-import pandas as pd\n-\n-\n-def _daily(points, events, ts_col, amount_col=None):\n-    \"\"\"Per customer and UTC day: number of events (and amount). Days that have a prediction but no event get 0.\"\"\"\n-    ev = events.assign(day=events[ts_col].dt.floor(\"D\"))\n-    agg = {\"n\": (ts_col, \"size\")}\n-    if amount_col:\n-        agg[\"amount\"] = (amount_col, \"sum\")\n-    per_day = ev.groupby([\"customer_id\", \"day\"]).agg(**agg).reset_index()\n-    pred_days = points[[\"customer_id\"]].assign(day=points[\"as_of\"].dt.floor(\"D\")).drop_duplicates()\n-    grid = pd.concat([per_day[[\"customer_id\", \"day\"]], pred_days]).drop_duplicates()\n-    daily = grid.merge(per_day, on=[\"customer_id\", \"day\"], how=\"left\").fillna(0)\n-    return daily.sort_values([\"customer_id\", \"day\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n-\n-\n-def _rolling(daily, cols, window):\n-    # daily buckets keep t"]
[53.824373, "i", "his fast; the window covers the last `window` including the prediction day\n-    rolled = (daily.set_index(\"day\").groupby(\"customer_id\")[cols]\n-              .rolling(window, closed=\"both\").sum().reset_index())\n-    return rolled\n-\n-\n-def activity_features(points, orders, tickets):\n-    out = points[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"]].copy()\n-    out[\"day\"] = out[\"as_of\"].dt.floor(\"D\")\n-\n-    od = _daily(points, orders, \"ordered_at\", \"amount_cents\")\n-    r7 = _rolling(od, [\"n\"], \"7D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"orders_7d\"})\n-    r30 = _rolling(od, [\"n\", \"amount\"], \"30D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"orders_30d\", \"amount\": \"spend_30d_cents\"})\n-    td = _daily(points, tickets, \"opened_at\")\n-    t30 = _rolling(td, [\"n\"], \"30D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"tickets_30d\"})\n-    for part in (r7, r30, t30):\n-        out = out.merge(part, on=[\"customer_id\", \"day\"], how=\"left\")\n-    for c in (\"orders_7d\", \"orders_30d\", \"spend_30d_cents\", \"tickets_30d\"):\n-        out[c] = out[c].fillna(0).astype(\"int64\")\n-\n-    # time since the last order strictly "]
[53.824455, "o", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[53.824527, "i", "before the prediction\n-    o = orders.sort_values(\"ordered_at\")[[\"customer_id\", \"ordered_at\"]]\n-    left = out[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"]].reset_index().sort_values(\"as_of\")\n-    last = pd.merge_asof(left, o, left_on=\"as_of\", right_on=\"ordered_at\", by=\"customer_id\",\n-                         allow_exact_matches=False).set_index(\"index\").sort_index()[\"ordered_at\"]\n-    out[\"days_since_last_order\"] = (out[\"as_of\"] - last).dt.total_seconds() / 86400\n-    return out.drop(columns=[\"day\"])\n+\"\"\"Activity features over trailing windows (orders, spend, tickets) and simple time‑since features.\n+\n+The original implementation aggregated events per calendar day and then used a closed=\"both\"\n+rolling window.  That unintentionally included events that occurred **after** the prediction\n+timestamp on the same day, violating the strict‑before rule described in `FEATURES.md`.\n+\n+The new implementation works directly with timestamps and uses `pd.merge_asof` to obtain\n+cumulative counts/sums strictly before each `as_of`.  For a "]
